{# A real 404 page, added 31 Aug 2026 — and it is load-bearing, not decoration.

   Cloudflare Pages serves 404.html from the site root for anything it cannot
   find. WITHOUT this file it answers with a generic fallback carrying a 200
   status, which means a missing asset looks like a successful response: the
   browser caches it, the edge caches it, and because `_headers` matches on
   path rather than content it gets marked long-lived. That is what left the
   live site unstyled on 31 Aug 2026 — a stylesheet URL requested seconds
   before its deploy landed returned HTML with a 200 and was cached at the
   edge for everyone.

   So: do not delete this file, and do not give it a permalink other than
   /404.html. Keep it plain and dependency-free. It must render correctly
   when the thing that is missing might be the stylesheet itself. #}

